    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0374" n="262" xml:id="pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/835</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-03"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3,
                        1919.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Polk</hi>: I must admit that I do not see
                    where we can get any money to pay these expenses after the 30th of June next,
                    but until then I am willing to pay out of the fund for National Security and
                    Defence the necessary amounts for the actual maintenance of our American railway
                    corps in Siberia. I understand from the enclosed letter that the present need is
                    for $117,000 dollars. I hope that you will use this letter as an authorization
                    for that amount and will keep me in touch with these things from month to
                    month.</p>
                <p>In haste,<lb/>Cordially and sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
